#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101018 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8de0dd63-23c6-5926-9e33-71e517949af2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Particular Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cea9e68-5ff1-55ff-83a9-77e47adb41fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "576" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097879} {:answer/id #uuid "28ccdcbc-7eba-50c4-8f39-13ef219dd95e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097880} {:answer/id #uuid "30857ed6-9876-5ffe-bddc-846b3bff7885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1152" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097881} {:answer/id #uuid "5d9f4e4a-d8bc-5580-9ad0-7ea4cc999386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097882} {:answer/id #uuid "699da513-aa51-566a-82a3-78281a6e8416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cea9e68-5ff1-55ff-83a9-77e47adb41fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "576" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097879} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a29c1fb-f5cd-5ed5-abda-25db6835320e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b0d07c3-7223-5d29-89dd-a42aeb1948e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-113627" :question/problem "The coefficient of ${x}^{7}$ in the expansion of ${(4+x)}^{9}$ is" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(4+x)}^{9},$ we have $a=4,$ $b=x,$ and $n=9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+x)^{9}=(\\frac{9}{0}){4}^{9}{x}^{0}+(\\frac{9}{1}){4}^{9-1}{x}^{1}+(\\frac{9}{2}){4}^{9-2}{x}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{9}{9}){4}^{9-9}{x}^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{7}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{9}{7}){4}^{9-7}{x}^{7}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the coefficient, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{9}{7}){4}^{9-7} & =36\\cdot {4}^{2} \\\\  & =36\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =576.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{7}$ is $576.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29896622-4bcb-5ad2-91d0-47c5911a619e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Few Terms of an Expansion With Negative Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "737ddc65-0f94-5ed3-938b-41d4cb4d3a74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{9}+9{s}^{8}t-36{s}^{7}t+…" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287677} {:answer/id #uuid "0a27fc2c-e4dc-5b22-8fca-723dce37cb43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{9}+9{s}^{8}t+72{s}^{7}t+…" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287678} {:answer/id #uuid "f366ba5b-4344-5f81-a7d7-7fb8fb6a32cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+36{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287679} {:answer/id #uuid "e87ddfaf-9c40-54d3-a5b5-0b866635285c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+42{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287680} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc3efcf-691e-59dd-95a1-9115ad47e7ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t-72{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f366ba5b-4344-5f81-a7d7-7fb8fb6a32cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+36{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287679} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b7d6e8e-1512-50b5-8b71-265233f37486" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26d64e14-48be-5cd9-8f9a-40fbb0ecc51d" :question/math-academy-id "q-12841" :question/problem "${(s-t)}^{9}=$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(s-t)}^{9},$ we have  $a=s,$ $b=-t,$ $n=9.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of ${(s-t)}^{9}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(s-t)}^{9} & =(\\frac{9}{0}){(s)}^{9}{(-t)}^{0}+(\\frac{9}{1}){(s)}^{9-1}{(-t)}^{1}+(\\frac{9}{2}){(s)}^{9-2}{(-t)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1{(s)}^{9}+9{(s)}^{8}{(-t)}^{1}+36{(s)}^{7}{(-t)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1({s}^{9})+9({s}^{8})(-t)+36({s}^{7})({t}^{2})+… \\\\  & ={s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+36{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29896622-4bcb-5ad2-91d0-47c5911a619e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Few Terms of an Expansion With Negative Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae5b2a67-3a62-5f8f-adc1-3b63cf3f0f0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256 - 256x + 96x^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098083} {:answer/id #uuid "c08b8be7-5e8c-5dcc-9c42-77f1a1826311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256 - 256x + 256x^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098084} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ac8326-588a-54e4-bf46-1384428e2ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256 - 96x + 96x^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098085} {:answer/id #uuid "652dc044-3dc7-51ce-9b85-2dd2d0ea618e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256 - 64x + 32x^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098086} {:answer/id #uuid "7940b976-9eee-5fc4-becf-22f10f4b520e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256 - 128x - 64x^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae5b2a67-3a62-5f8f-adc1-3b63cf3f0f0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "256 - 256x + 96x^{2} + ⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098083} :answer-field/id #uuid "68931d1c-fcdb-52cf-9d9e-b6bb6daa6d6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1580f8d4-9b2d-526c-a1a3-3117f94565e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-135896" :question/problem "$(4-x)^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of $(4-x)^{4},$ we have  $a=4,$ $b=-x,$ $n=4.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of $(4-x)^{4}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(4-x)}^{4} & =(\\frac{4}{0}){(4)}^{4}{(-x)}^{0}+(\\frac{4}{1}){(4)}^{4-1}{(-x)}^{1}+(\\frac{4}{2}){(4)}^{4-2}{(-x)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1{(4)}^{4}+4{(4)}^{3}{(-x)}^{1}+6{(4)}^{2}{(-x)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =256-256x+96{x}^{2}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29896622-4bcb-5ad2-91d0-47c5911a619e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Few Terms of an Expansion With Negative Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d55296b-5aac-5d71-9f25-b360d582e92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81-108x-9{x}^{2}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287684} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6df536-6d21-56d3-922d-f10bfb498344" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81+27x+18{x}^{2}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287685} {:answer/id #uuid "2094cff9-99e6-5835-97b3-953308ea58a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81-108x+54{x}^{2}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287686} {:answer/id #uuid "5173a1f7-9360-56df-94fb-7347c2d3d7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81-27x+54{x}^{2}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287687} {:answer/id #uuid "259e697b-436f-58ea-92b5-8bc6ced2ef5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81-108x+9{x}^{2}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2094cff9-99e6-5835-97b3-953308ea58a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81-108x+54{x}^{2}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287686} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ecae32b-8e41-5446-95a6-c4a7301808da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a98cc425-2183-5f47-adb9-ffa5ea8d3826" :question/math-academy-id "q-136011" :question/problem "$(3-x)^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of $(3-x)^{4},$ we have  $a=3,$ $b=-x,$ $n=4.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of $(3-x)^{4}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(3-x)}^{4} & =(\\frac{4}{0}){(3)}^{4}{(-x)}^{0}+(\\frac{4}{1}){(3)}^{4-1}{(-x)}^{1}+(\\frac{4}{2}){(3)}^{4-2}{(-x)}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1{(3)}^{4}+4{(3)}^{3}{(-x)}^{1}+6{(3)}^{2}{(-x)}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =81-108x+54{x}^{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8de0dd63-23c6-5926-9e33-71e517949af2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Particular Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5663ebb-e56f-550b-a880-6e7d45446d25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "908" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287691} {:answer/id #uuid "13a0f83f-28b2-582f-bb78-acd923a383e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "880" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287692} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b5f27d-5a1d-5fa0-8f5b-772b8e15357a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "702" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287693} {:answer/id #uuid "d611b0ca-b30a-5d1b-ad4b-ff28f17fd8fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287694} {:answer/id #uuid "f3688491-67a7-520d-8cf9-14d761f08153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "560" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9b5f27d-5a1d-5fa0-8f5b-772b8e15357a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "702" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287693} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5768e4a-4307-59ef-ac7a-aac421db0dd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eb8bdf03-c0dc-5ef8-8cc5-e037aae4166c" :question/math-academy-id "q-18621" :question/problem "The coefficient of ${x}^{22}$ in the expansion of ${(3+{x}^{2})}^{13}$ is" :question/worked-solution "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(3+{x}^{2})}^{13},$ we have $a=3,$ $b={x}^{2},$ and $n=13.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(3+{x}^{2})}^{13}=(\\frac{13}{0}){3}^{13}{({x}^{2})}^{0}+(\\frac{13}{1}){3}^{13-1}{({x}^{2})}^{1}+(\\frac{13}{2}){3}^{13-2}{({x}^{2})}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{13}{13}){3}^{13-13}{({x}^{2})}^{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{22}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{13}{11}){3}^{13-11}{({x}^{2})}^{11}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying this term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{13}{11}){3}^{13-11}{({x}^{2})}^{11} & =78\\cdot {3}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{22} \\\\  & =78\\cdot 9\\cdot {x}^{22} \\\\  & =702{x}^{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{22}$ is $702.$"}]}
